# EVERY INSTANCE OF EVERY COMPUTATION THIS MODEL PERFORMS, WITH A VERDICT ON WHETHER IT MAY BE
# PERFORMED. One row per (site, examined item): which arithmetic, which layer of which filing,
# whether the operands are there and commensurable, and a sentence saying what is in the way.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THIS IS THE RELATION examples/readiness/main.rs IS A VIEW OF, AND IT ANSWERS A DIFFERENT
#    QUESTION FROM checks/all.sqlc. A check says the document contradicts the model. This says
#    you cannot compute here at all -- which is not a defect in the document and not a pass
#    either. Reporting the second as the first accuses a filer of a gap they told you about.
#
# ⭐⭐ THREE VERDICTS, NOT TWO. `computable`, `suspended`, `not comparable`. The middle one is
#    the one a boolean cannot hold, and it is the common case: sixteen of thirty-six layers
#    cannot sum their shares because somebody declined to measure one.
#
# ⛔ THE CONTRACT EVERY SITE KEEPS: one plain SELECT, no leading WITH, returning exactly
#   `(site, filing, layer, verdict, detail)`, with `verdict` NULL only on the roster row that
#   says a site examined nothing. Same shape as checks/, same reason.
-- arithmetic/roster.sqlc joined to each site's own population.
:union(ALL arithmetic/remainder.sqlc,
           arithmetic/shares_sum.sqlc,
           arithmetic/shares_bounded.sqlc,
           arithmetic/whole_multiple.sqlc,
           arithmetic/draw_bounded.sqlc,
           arithmetic/exposure_bounded.sqlc,
           arithmetic/time_slack_derived.sqlc,
           arithmetic/filed_remainder.sqlc,
           arithmetic/fusion_sum.sqlc)
